-- title:
--   Integrality of j(mathsf q) over A[j(mathsf q^q)] in the level field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$) which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79); that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the intermediate field `xHFunctionField` of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(\mathsf q)\!)/\mathbb{Q}$ attached to the level $(q\ell)^2M'$ and to the subgroup `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^{\times}$, the latter being the kernel of the unit-group reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` for the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul (q*ℓ) M'`. Let further $A$ be a commutative ring which is an algebra over both $L$ and $K$, compatibly (scalar tower $A \to L \to K$). The assertion is the existence of three facts: that $j(\mathsf q) :=$ `coeffEmb L jq` lies in $K$, where `jq` $= \mathsf q^{-1}\cdot$ (the power series `jNumQ`) is the $q$-expansion of the $j$-invariant; that its image under [`ModularCurve.qExpand L q`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), the substitution multiplying all Laurent exponents by $q$ (so $j(\mathsf q^{q})$), lies in $K$; that this second element of $K$ is nonzero; and, with that nonvanishing in force, that $j(\mathsf q)$, viewed in $K$, belongs to [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) of $j(\mathsf q^{q})$, i.e. $j(\mathsf q)$ is integral over the $A$-subalgebra $A[j(\mathsf q^{q})]$ of $K$.
--
--   This is the classical integrality of $j$ over $\mathbb{Z}[j\circ(\mathsf q\mapsto \mathsf q^{q})]$, expressed inside the base-changed level-$(q\ell)^2M'$ function field and in the form needed for the finite chart of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve, whose chart ring is the integral closure of $A[j(\mathsf q^{q})]$ in $K$. It is used in the analysis of maximal ideals and of the reduction of $j$-values, via [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin).
